 Server-Sent Events stream of the run's tool-call progress, token deltas, and lifecycle events. Designed for dashboards and thick clients that want to attach/detach without losing state.
 
+When `features.run_event_replay.supported` and `fanout` are true, each viewer
+has an independent cursor. Frames include a numeric SSE `id` and matching
+`sequence` in their JSON payload. Send `Last-Event-ID` on reconnect to receive
+only newer frames. Disconnecting one viewer does not remove another viewer or
+the retained event history.
+
+Replay is in-process and bounded to 1,024 events / 4 MiB per run, with a shared
+64 MiB / 16,384-record adapter budget. An out-of-range cursor returns HTTP 409
+`run_replay_gap`. A connected viewer that falls behind receives an `error` event
+with that code, then closes. Poll run status for the final output and current
+`event_cursor` / `event_replay_floor`; do not render a truncated replay as a
+complete transcript. A client may explicitly resume from the current cursor
+while labelling earlier live output as unavailable. Gateway restart does not
+preserve the event log; durable run status is the recovery source.
+
+
